tes later - the boundary trap the find-routine skill warns about), and JSR $9508 at CPU $9401 and $94D3 (prgRom 0x1401/0x14D3) confirms $9508 as the entry. Those callers sit inside the routine at $93FC, itself reached from the task dispatcher JSR $8E04 at $92C8 whose table at $92CB has $93FC as an entry, called from the per-frame/task routine $92B0 (called at $86E9 and $AF8F). PROOF by ledgered write: write_memory prgRom 0x2691 (byte1 of the first World 1-1 layout record) $81 -> $01 (ledger seq 1, reason 'clear page-advance flag of the first World 1-1 layout record'), reset_emulator, then started a game to World 1-1. The decoder built the object stream one page earlier: the normally empty first screen (hill + bush + ground + cloud only) now showed a ? block in the sky, a brick row with two ? blocks, a lone ? block at the far left and a green pipe at x~200. undo_edit restored $81. So the byte at prgRom 0x2691 is read and acted on by this routine.\",\"confidence\":1,\"rom_origins\":[{\"mem\":\"prgRom\",\"offset\":5384,\"length\":129,\"notes\":\"CPU $9508-$9588, the area object decoder (prgRom 0x1508)\"}],\"source\":\"trace and disassembly\",\"recorded\":true,\"event_type\":\"mapping_discovered\"}"}
